From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 21:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: cix: diagnose VPU clock before MMIO

Log the resolved VPU clock's actual rate and enable state immediately after
enabling it.  Fail probe with a benign error at that point because returning
success would let mvx_dev_probe() reach mvx_hwreg_get_core_mask() and fault on
the same inaccessible VPU registers.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [debug]
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
index 600bf3d13..058360dc5 100755
--- a/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/cix/dev/mvx_dev.c
@@ -1222,6 +1222,11 @@ static int mvx_pm_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
         return ret;
     }
 
+    dev_err(dev, "MVXDIAG: vpu_clk rate=%lu rcsu=%d rstc=%d\n",
+            clk_get_rate(ctx->clk),
+            ctx->rcsu_rstc ? 1 : 0, ctx->rstc ? 1 : 0);
+    return -ENODEV; /* MVXDIAG: fail probe before any VPU MMIO */
+
     /*
      * Order matters: deassert the reset BEFORE enabling the IRQ.  Otherwise
      * the IRQ can fire mid-reset (when the device is not yet fully out of
-- 
2.47.3
